{"id": "EUVD-2026-80602", "enisaUuid": "cedaa887-0426-3f96-84a3-e2a3b40f55da", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndmaengine: fsl-edma: tracing: no ptr dereference during log output\n\nThe fsl edma events store a pointer to a struct fsl_edma_engine in the\nringbuffer and dereference it when a log entry is printed. At this time,\nthe pointer may no longer be valid.\n\nEvent injection can be used to trigger a crash:\n\n$ cd /sys/kernel/tracing\n$ echo 'value = 0' > events/fsl_edma/edma_writeb/inject\n$ cat trace\n\nThe log output needs only edma->membase. Add a membase field at the end\nof the event and use the new field for log output. Keep the existing\nfields for backward compatibility.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:33:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:56:08", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ef02cd3807f39ae1dbc924788d8fa6a85334c435", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d382aaf5fed38c6dd2e0cc710d97cb81d660ffa7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2a3801ae5c344473e648006c5b03a9216ac54a6a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2ea04dca8e627f722caa7a2037cfbae0257f3501"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2hx9-3cqh-fcjj", "CVE-2026-89994"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0f351d56-d04d-36a3-9f37-17fdab5ae63c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "11102d0c343ba06ddd303f2503c0ce46d70052f2 <d382aaf5fed38c6dd2e0cc710d97cb81d660ffa7"}, {"id": "160d2da0-2422-35c0-88e2-97e3d3f254a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "164a50de-80cd-38d0-8912-ee298e4b3497", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "2a83e61f-d288-3f32-9ced-85cfdfc70f33", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "11102d0c343ba06ddd303f2503c0ce46d70052f2 <ef02cd3807f39ae1dbc924788d8fa6a85334c435"}, {"id": "2f57e9c9-4f92-3cfc-b1a3-8eece12f60c6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3d094873-7e4d-328b-895c-f8487b2d3572", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "11102d0c343ba06ddd303f2503c0ce46d70052f2 <2a3801ae5c344473e648006c5b03a9216ac54a6a"}, {"id": "a13f63a8-37cb-3650-a644-a298a3a11852", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "c15c5a59-2dbd-30f2-8d91-8c8066d755cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "11102d0c343ba06ddd303f2503c0ce46d70052f2 <2ea04dca8e627f722caa7a2037cfbae0257f3501"}, {"id": "d82879e3-c9d3-3850-82b5-701374fb1526", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.10"}, {"id": "f6306a20-5e71-3b12-a663-69cdf9f44eed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "cff1c5c5-6354-3a6d-a38a-fd1069eeee5a", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}